  "summary": "Selected evidence records: FuXi is documented as a terminal AI coding agent built in Go, shipped as a single static binary with no runtime dependencies, positioned as a provider-agnostic alternative to Claude Code. The agent is described as running a Think → Act → Verify loop: it reasons about a task, acts with built-in tools, inspects results, and iterates until the work is verified.",
